@ [method] seven_fold_specification_explosion

& [Fold1IdentityAndPurpose] distinguishes ledger from frame semantics
  + the ledger is an append-only content-addressed custody layer for already typed shared-attention frames and operation outcomes
  + one session names one explicit current head while every retained frame remains retrievable by full SHA-256 digest
  + the purpose is compact exact reentry without resending the complete base frame on every operation
  + ledger custody does not sign SOP assert truth authorize effects or replace frame validation

& [Fold2ActorsAuthorityAndVisibility] prevents hidden server authority
  + the caller chooses ledger and session identities and supplies an initial complete validated frame
  + later apply calls bind expected session sequence head generation head digest and policy through the underlying operation forms
  + the core runtime remains transition authority and the ledger may only record its exact typed response
  + every successful ledger command returns ledger digest session sequence head identity and event reference
  + inspect read-frame and read-event operations expose complete retained state by exact identity

& [Fold3DataAndRelationships] forms the append-only graph
  + AttentionLedger contains profile ledger identity frames keyed by frame digest sessions events and ledger digest
  + AttentionSessionState contains session identity sequence current head digest generation status ordered event references and session digest
  + AttentionLedgerEvent binds session sequence command digest response digest predecessor head optional successor head disposition and event digest
  + AttentionContinuation binds the exact successor ledger digest session head and latest event
  + frames are immutable values and a digest collision with unequal bytes is refused

& [Fold4CommandsAndTransitions] closes the initial runtime
  + OPEN validates the supplied frame and creates a new session whose first appended event establishes sequence one
  + APPLY resolves the current frame from the ledger and executes reconcile compact prepare or settle without caller repetition of the base frame
  + APPLY requires exact expected sequence and head digest before semantic dispatch
  + every admitted attempt appends one event and advances session sequence exactly once
  + applied compaction prepared candidate or sealed settlement changes the head to the exact returned frame
  + buffered incomplete deferred revision-required or semantic refusal records the outcome while retaining the prior head
  + INSPECT returns one session continuation READ_FRAME returns one exact frame and READ_EVENT returns one exact event

& [Fold5ConcurrencyBackpressureAndReentry] keeps updates linearizable
  + pure core execution accepts an immutable ledger and returns either one complete successor ledger plus result or one fault and no successor
  + a local MCP host serializes process-local mutations and still requires compare-and-set bindings from every caller
  + simultaneous callers from one observed head cannot both silently advance it because the second becomes stale
  + core backpressure remains distinct from ledger staleness and retains the unchanged head
  + a continuation is a compact locator and proof handle rather than a replacement for inspectable retained records

& [Fold6HonestySecurityAndProof] guards history
  + ledger frame session event and root digests are recomputed and validated at every command
  + unknown frame event or session identity duplicate session stale sequence stale head bad digest and illegal operation state refuse without successor
  + event identity and response digest make recorded failure success and backpressure distinguishable
  + no update deletes rewrites or reclassifies a historical frame or event
  + serialization rejects unknown fields and deterministic replay produces equal successor ledger bytes
  + process restart loss is declared and never represented as durable persistence

& [Fold7PruningGrowthAndPhaseLock] selects a local in-memory vertical slice
  + retain pure ledger forms digest validation open apply inspect read-frame read-event and one separately named stateless-schema stateful-process MCP adapter
  + retain only reality-frame reconcile compact prepare and settle under APPLY
  + prune DreamFrame session custody persistence files database network listeners replication authentication leases cleanup deletion compaction encryption and deployment
  + later layers may store the same canonical ledger in SQLite RocksDB or a replicated service under separate authority
  + [exhaustion_state] is seven_fold_phase_locked_for_in_memory_reentry_P0

& [Flowchart] is the session execution surface
  + L0 create empty ledger
  + L1 OPEN session with complete validated frame
  + L2 return continuation handle
  + L3 caller proposes compact APPLY against exact handle
  + L4 resolve full frame and execute core transition
  + L5 append outcome event and optionally advance head
  + L6 return new continuation and core response
  + L7 later caller INSPECT READ_FRAME or re-enters at L3

& [DualHemisphereReview] reconciles stream and audit
  + holistic side sees one continuing semantic trajectory and can resume it by a small handle
  + delineating side sees immutable frame objects explicit event edges compare-and-set heads and complete readback
  + reconciliation provides a shared junction without confusing convenience state with authority or persistence

& [ResidualFrontier] remains explicit
  + large result payloads remain until compact response projection is separately specified
  + in-memory process state does not survive restart
  + multi-process transport needs authentication durable ordering and recovery
  + DreamFrame branches need their own ledger identity and merge policy
